# Phase 5: Pages & Component Implementation Checklists

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Single Source of Truth**: this file is the canonical inventory of pages,
> sections, child components, and page-level support files. No other file tracks
> page/component progress.
>
> **Page Completion Rule**: tick a page (`- [x]`) **if and only if** every child
> component and every page-level task is complete and verified.

## Page-level mandatory tasks

Every page must include all six:

1. `page.tsx` — view and layout assembly
2. `loading.tsx` — streaming skeleton
3. `error.tsx` — nested boundary with a recovery action
4. `generateMetadata` / `metadata` — title, description, OG/Twitter
5. JSON-LD structured data appropriate to the page type
6. `generateStaticParams()` — when the route is dynamic or localized

## Component acceptance (applies to every component)

- [ ] Renders all states: default, loading, empty, error.
- [ ] Keyboard reachable; `axe` scan clean.
- [ ] All visible copy comes from the dictionary (no hard-coded strings).
- [ ] Works in RTL; mixed-direction values use `dir="auto"`.
- [ ] No overflow at the smallest and largest breakpoint.
- [ ] Unit test (or story) covers the happy path and one edge case.
- [ ] Uses semantic tokens only — no raw palette class, arbitrary value, or
      inline style.

